WEBVTT

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.930
Good sessions are won before they start.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.210
Here are the three things to prepare.

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:14.610
First, the purpose. Finish this sentence for yourself: “After this session, we will have…”

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:18.130
For example: “…a first version of our purpose statement.”

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:22.290
Or: “…agreed how we make our three most common decisions.”

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:26.290
If you can’t finish the sentence, you’re not ready to invite people yet.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.370
Second, the invitation.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.910
Tell your team why you’re doing this, in your own words, and what you hope for.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.830
Keep it short and human.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:40.530
Something like: “We’ve been busy delivering, and we’ve never really talked about how we want to work together.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.570
I’d like us to spend two hours on that.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:45.470
No preparation needed, just come curious.”

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:50.350
If you like, send the short intro video from formyourteam.dk along with it.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:54.690
Avoid making it sound like a fix for a problem person, or a hidden agenda.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:58.330
People can smell that from far away, and they’ll stay guarded.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:05.350
Third, the room. If you meet in person, book a room with wall space, and print the canvases in a big size.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.970
Bring plenty of post-its and thick markers, because thin pens make people write long sentences.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:14.986
Arrange chairs in a circle or a horseshoe, not facing a screen.

00:01:15.036 --> 00:01:21.706
If you meet online, copy the Miro template, test it beforehand, and ask everyone to keep their camera on if they can.

00:01:21.756 --> 00:01:26.726
Online, give extra time for writing quietly, and be stricter with time boxes.

00:01:26.776 --> 00:01:29.426
And one more thing: protect the time.

00:01:29.476 --> 00:01:33.246
No laptops for email, and no “I’ll just join for the first half.”

00:01:33.296 --> 00:01:37.063
If the session is important enough to run, it’s important enough to show up for.

